   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend part P of chapter 54 of the laws of 2016, relating to\nutilizing reverses in the mortgage insurance fund for various housing\npurposes, in relation to administering local programs to repair or replace\nmobile or manufactured homes damaged as a result of ice jam flooding",
    "basePrintNo": "S7714",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S7714-2017",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Add Part P §9-a, Chap 54 of 2016",
    "lawSection": "Housing",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S7714\n\nSPONSOR: LITTLE\n \nTITLE OF BILL:  An act to amend part P of chapter 54 of the laws of\n2016, relating to utilizing reverses in the mortgage insurance fund for\nvarious housing purposes, in relation to administering local programs to\nrepair or replace mobile or manufactured homes damaged as a result of\nice jam flooding\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThe bill would amend the eligibility requirements for the existing Homes\nand Community Renewal Mobile and Manufactured Home Replacement Program\nto serve residents of Underwood Estates that own their homes, but lease\nthe land, as the current program only serves individuals that own both\nthe home and the land.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 would amend the Part P of chapter 54 of the laws of 2016, by\nadding a new section 9-a to permit eligible units of local government or\nnot for profit corporations with substantial experience in affordable\nhousing may apply to administer local programs to repair or replace\ndilapidated mobile or manufactured homes that were damaged as a result\nof ice jam flooding of Saranac River between December 1, 2017 and Janu-\nary 31, 2018.\n\nThis Section would permit such eligible applicant to repair or replace\ndamaged mobile or manufactured homes that are sited on land owned or\nleased by the homeowner. Further, this Section eliminates the $500,000\nfunding cap on an award to a single eligible applicant and the require-\nment that homes built with funds pursuant to this Section be energy star\nrated to facilitate the expedited manufacture and siting of homes in the\nUnderwood Estates Mobile Park.\n\n \nEXISTING LAW:\n\nThe existing Mobile and Manufactured Home Replacement Program is avail-\nable only to replace mobile or manufactured homes It also caps the total\nawards for a single eligible applicant at $500,000 and required that\nhomes built with program funds be energy star rated.\n\n \nBUDGET IMPLICATIONS:\n\nThis legislation is not expected to have an impact on the budget\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis bill would take effect immediately\n",
